# Rust / Tauri
src-tauri/target

# Agent tooling, installed per-machine rather than vendored (~24MB of skill
# files). Reinstallable, so it stays out of the repo. `.mcp.json` is tracked
# deliberately — it is machine-independent and shared, not an install artifact.
.agents/
.claude/
_bmad/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# BMAD UX working scratch — screenshots, Playwright CLI logs, and mockup
# iterations. Regenerable exploration output, not deliverables;
# the DESIGN.md/EXPERIENCE.md/mockups and reports under _bmad-output are tracked.
#
# .memlog.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is a workflow run's append-only
# working memory — `_bmad/scripts/memlog.py` has no edit or delete subcommand by
# design — and the bmad-* Update intents resume from it as "the authority on what
# was decided", not from the rendered artifact. It is not a deliverable, but it is
# not regenerable either: lose it and the artifact can never be re-distilled.
**/.working/
**/.playwright-cli/
.bmad-loop/runs/
.bmad-loop/cache/
.bmad-loop/policy.toml

# Timestamped backup snapshots the docs-scan workflow writes when it
# regenerates docs/project-scan-report.json. Git already versions the
# canonical file, so these archive copies stay out of the repo.
docs/.archive/

# Local agent tooling — machine-specific paths and working data.
# `.bmad-loop/` is not blanket-ignored: `bmad_loop_hook.py` and
# `profiles/grok.toml` are tracked (same as My-Love / Google-Drive-MCP).
# Per-run state and the per-machine policy stay ignored.
.bmad-loop/archive/
.codex/
_bmad/render/

# Grok CLI (bmad-loop adapter). Untracked, like .claude/ and _bmad/, except
# the hook registration. Grok 1.0.30 discovers repo-scoped skills even when
# gitignored; worktree checkouts get `.grok/skills` and `.grok/hooks` via
# seed_files in .bmad-loop/profiles/grok.toml. `init` writes the hook file
# only once, and worktree reuse never re-seeds it, so the SessionEnd omission
# that keeps grok sessions alive is tracked.
.grok/*
!.grok/hooks/
.grok/hooks/*
!.grok/hooks/bmad-loop.json

# Playwright CLI output (may contain credentials)
.playwright-cli/
